# MineDigital360

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform — and the reason each line is here
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan

# tfstate is excluded because it is the one Terraform artefact that routinely
# contains SECRETS IN PLAINTEXT — every attribute of every resource, including
# the ones the provider marks sensitive. A repository with a committed tfstate
# has published its own credentials, and the commit history keeps them after
# the file is deleted. This programme has no remote backend yet (ADR-004: the
# evidence window creates and destroys, so there is nothing long-lived to
# track), and when it acquires one, the backend is where state belongs.

*.tfvars
!example.tfvars
# tfvars carries the variable VALUES — account IDs, subscription GUIDs, org
# names. The example file is allowed through on purpose so the shape is
# documented without the contents.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials — belt and braces behind FF-03
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*
credentials
*_rsa
*_ed25519

# FF-03 fails the build on a static credential SHAPE anywhere in the tree.
# These lines stop such a file being staged in the first place. Neither
# replaces the other: the ignore list prevents the accident, the fitness
# function catches the one that gets past it — for example a credential
# pasted into a .md file, which no ignore pattern would ever cover.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker / plant runtime
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
plant/scada/project/*
!plant/scada/project/README.md
# FUXA writes its live project state into this directory. The README is the
# build instruction and is tracked; the generated project is not, until it is
# deliberately exported.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# .DS_Store is deliberately absent — there is no macOS anywhere near this
# programme, and an ignore file padded with rules for platforms nobody uses
# is a file nobody reads.
